# Claude Code Plugins
# Format: plugin@marketplace  (or a bare plugin name to let Claude resolve it)
# Used by: scripts/install_claude.sh  (dotfiles install --claude)
#
# One plugin per marketplace in claude/marketplaces.list, plus the two the
# bootstrap itself needs. Anything else goes in claude/plugins.local.list
# (gitignored) or is installed per-project.
#
# Marketplace ids come from each repo's .claude-plugin/marketplace.json, not
# from the repo name -- compound-engineering-plugin registers itself as
# "compound-engineering-plugin". The installer falls back to resolving a bare
# plugin name if the qualified id does not match, so a renamed marketplace
# upstream does not break the bootstrap.

superpowers@superpowers-marketplace
compound-engineering@compound-engineering-plugin

# Required by the QMD/Obsidian bootstrap, not a preference:
#   recall                -> extract-sessions.py, driven by the Stop hook
#   sync-claude-sessions  -> populates $VAULT_DIR/Claude-Sessions, which
#                            setup_qmd registers as the "sessions" collection
recall-skill@personal-os-skills
sync-claude-sessions-skill@personal-os-skills

# To discover what a marketplace offers:
#   claude plugin list --available
#   claude plugin details <name>     # component inventory + token cost
